  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "multi_choice",
      "title_markdown": "Select **all** correct statements about the vector (cross) product $\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}$.",
      "instruction": "Select all correct options.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 1,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "It is anti-commutative: $\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b} = -(\\vec{b} \\times \\vec{a})$.",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "Its magnitude equals the area of the parallelogram formed by $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$.",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "It is zero when $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are parallel.",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "The result is a scalar.",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q1_opt_1",
        "q1_opt_2",
        "q1_opt_3"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Idea.** The cross product yields a vector perpendicular to both inputs.\n\n- $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = -(\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{a})$ (anti-commutative) — **correct**.\n- $|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|$ is the parallelogram area — **correct**.\n- For parallel vectors $\\sin\\theta = 0$, so the product is the zero vector — **correct**.\n- The result is a **vector**, not a scalar (that is the dot product) — **wrong**.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "title_markdown": "Evaluate the definite integral $$\\int_1^{2} 3x^2 \\, dx.$$",
      "instruction": "Choose the one correct option.",
