        {
          "id": "q2_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$3$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q2_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Step 1 — Antiderivative.** $$\\int 3x^2\\,dx = x^3.$$\n\n**Step 2 — Apply limits $1$ to $2$.** $$\\left[x^3\\right]_1^{2} = 2^3 - 1^3.$$\n\n**Step 3 — Simplify.** $$= 8 - 1 = 7.$$\n\n**Answer.** $7$.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "true_false",
      "title_markdown": "Two lines in space with direction ratios $(a_1, b_1, c_1)$ and $(a_2, b_2, c_2)$ are perpendicular if $a_1 a_2 + b_1 b_2 + c_1 c_2 = 0$.",
      "instruction": "State whether the statement is True or False.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 3,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q3_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "True",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q3_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "False",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q3_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Idea.** The angle between two lines is found from the dot product of their direction vectors.\n\nPerpendicular lines have $\\cos 90^\\circ = 0$, which forces $a_1 a_2 + b_1 b_2 + c_1 c_2 = 0$. The statement is **true**.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "title_markdown": "The magnitude of the vector $\\vec{a} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$ is:",
      "instruction": "Choose the one correct option.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 4,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q4_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "$3$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q4_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "$5$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q4_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "$9$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q4_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$\\sqrt{5}$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q4_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Rule — magnitude.** $$|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{a_x^2 + a_y^2 + a_z^2}.$$\n\n**Step 1 — Square and add components.** $1^2 + 2^2 + 2^2 = 1 + 4 + 4 = 9$.\n\n**Step 2 — Take the square root.** $$|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{9} = 3.$$\n\n**Answer.** $|\\vec{a}| = 3$.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "title_markdown": "The principal value of $\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$ is:",
      "instruction": "Choose the one correct option.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 5,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q5_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "$\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q5_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q5_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q5_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q5_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Idea.** $\\cos^{-1}x$ returns the angle in the principal range $[0, \\pi]$ whose cosine is $x$.\n\n**Step 1.** We need $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi]$ with $\\cos\\theta = -\\tfrac{1}{2}$.\n\n**Step 2.** Since $\\cos\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3} \\in [0,\\pi]$, $$\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}.$$\n\n**Answer.** $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "true_false",
      "title_markdown": "For a definite integral, swapping the limits changes the sign: $\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx = -\\int_b^a f(x)\\,dx$.",
      "instruction": "State whether the statement is True or False.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 6,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q6_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "True",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q6_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "False",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q6_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Idea.** Reversing the direction of integration reverses the sign of every signed-area element.\n\nFormally $\\int_a^b f = F(b) - F(a)$ and $\\int_b^a f = F(a) - F(b)$, which are negatives of each other. The statement is **true**.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "title_markdown": "A fair coin is tossed $4$ times. Using the binomial distribution, the probability of getting exactly $2$ heads is:",
      "instruction": "Choose the one correct option.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 7,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q7_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "$0.375$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q7_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "$0.25$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q7_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "$0.5$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q7_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$0.125$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q7_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Given.** $n = 4$ tosses, $p = 0.5$, want $P(X = 2)$.\n\n**Step 1 — Binomial formula.** $$P(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}.$$\n\n**Step 2 — Substitute.** $$P(X=2) = \\binom{4}{2}(0.5)^2(0.5)^2 = 6 \\times (0.5)^4.$$\n\n**Step 3 — Simplify.** $$= 6 \\times 0.0625 = 0.375.$$\n\n**Answer.** $0.375$.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "type": "true_false",
      "title_markdown": "If $A$ and $B$ are independent events with $P(B) > 0$, then $P(A \\mid B) = P(A)$.",
      "instruction": "State whether the statement is True or False.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "points": 10,
      "sort_order": 8,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "q8_opt_1",
          "slot_position": 1,
          "label_markdown": "True",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "id": "q8_opt_2",
          "slot_position": 2,
          "label_markdown": "False",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q8_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Idea.** Conditional probability is $P(A\\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}$.\n\nFor independent events $P(A\\cap B) = P(A)P(B)$, so $P(A\\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(A)P(B)}{P(B)} = P(A)$. Independence means $B$ gives no information about $A$. The statement is **true**.",
      "source_style_ref": "Droid-authored (exam-grade)"
    },
    {
